<title>USA: U.S. milk production dips in September - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. milk production dips in September - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said milk production in the 22 major producing states was 10.7 billion pounds in September, down one percent from a year ago and off from 11.0 billion pounds in August.</p>
<p>In a monthly report, USDA said on a daily basis, milk production has been below 1995 levels every month this year.</p>
<p>It said production per cow in the 22 major states averaged 1,341 pounds in September, 10 pounds above September 1995.</p>
<p>The number of cows on farms declined for the 13th month in a row to 7.96 million head, 100,000 head less than the same period a year ago and 8,000 head less than August, USDA said.</p>
